HUD button arrangement setting, game.hudButtonLayout = original | vita (the Vita defaults to
vita). With vita, the B button and the X button of the main HUD (zelda_game_image) trade places
once, when the HUD is built: with A on cross, B on circle and X on square the icons then sit as
the buttons do on the console (square left, circle right, triangle on top) instead of the
GameCube pad's places (B lower left, X right). When circle confirms (A on circle, B on cross) the
original arrangement already has the cross below and left of the circle, and is kept.

Each button is three children of the button parent: the letter (bbtn_n, xbtn_n), the item
(item_b_n, item_x_n) and the action text (b_text_n, x_text_n). Each B pane goes where its X
counterpart was and the reverse. The item panes are only shown and hidden by the game, so they
are translated once; the letter and text panes are placed on every draw from their CPaneMgr's
start position, so that start position moves. Every distance is the one between the two panes
of a pair, read from the layout: no number from the disc is in the code. Item icons, counts, the
lantern meter and the sparkles follow because they are children of, or measured from, those
panes.

Presentation only: the pad mapping, what each button does and every other screen are untouched.
With original, or on other platforms (default original), nothing moves.

